---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";

const sections = [
  { href: "#pollution", label: "Pollution" },
  { href: "#climate", label: "Climate" },
  { href: "#flower-moon", label: "Killers of the Flower Moon" },
];
---

<Base
  title="The Crimes — Long Knife"
  description="Pollution, climate destruction, and a century of killings. The crimes the Kochs and Big Oil committed on the Osage Reservation — and how they made them legal."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Behind every great fortune"
    title="THE CRIMES"
    subtitle="They didn't just steal the oil. They poisoned the land, broke the climate, and — long before that — got away with murder."
  />

  <!-- Section jump nav -->
  <nav
    class="sticky top-[57px] z-30 border-y border-white/10 bg-[color-mix(in_srgb,var(--color-ink)_88%,transparent)] backdrop-blur-md"
    aria-label="Crimes on this page"
  >
    <ul
      class="mx-auto flex max-w-5xl items-center justify-center gap-6 overflow-x-auto px-6 py-4 text-[10px] tracking-[0.25em] whitespace-nowrap text-white/60 uppercase sm:gap-10 sm:text-xs"
    >
      {
        sections.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <a class="transition-colors hover:text-[var(--color-red)]" href={s.href}>
              {s.label}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <!-- ============================ POLLUTION ============================ -->
  <section id="pollution" class="scroll-mt-32 px-6 pt-14 pb-12 sm:pt-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.4em] text-[var(--color-red)] uppercase">
        Crime One
      </p>
      <h2
        class="mt-4 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-5xl leading-[0.95] tracking-tight sm:text-7xl"
      >
        Pollution Crimes
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
        Charlie Koch didn't steal all the Osage oil. Some his crews dumped into
        creeks and rivers. Koch let pipes crack, spewing murderous poisons. Koch
        Oil was indicted for over <strong class="text-[var(--color-bone)]"
          >315 counts of felonious criminal polluting</strong
        >. And walked away smelling like a rose.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="relative my-12">
    <img
      src="/oily-water.jpg"
      alt="A pool of crude-fouled water, a wellhead reflected in its black surface, on the Osage Reservation."
      class="h-[45vh] w-full object-cover sm:h-[60vh]"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </figure>

  <section class="px-6 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
      <p>
        The crime spree continued. We reveal the inside story of how Koch bought
        and bullied his way out of these crimes &mdash; from having Koch thugs
        impersonate an FBI agent to terrorize a whistleblower, to running
        counterintelligence operations against the Feds, to slipping millions
        through &ldquo;Triad,&rdquo; a corporate front.
      </p>
      <p>
        How did he get away with it? The Kochs bought themselves a Congress and
        pleasured a Supreme Court Justice. And they simply had Congress and the
        Court <em>make their crimes legal</em>.
      </p>
      <p
        class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-red)] pl-6 font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-2xl text-white italic sm:text-3xl"
      >
        Capone never thought of that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 pb-24">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-px bg-white/10 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/koch-warning-sign.jpg"
          alt="A weathered Koch high-pressure petroleum warning sign fallen in the brush."
          class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/pumpjack-overcast.jpg"
          alt="A derelict pump jack under a flat grey sky, a figure crouched at its base."
          class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/abandoned-wells-poster.jpg"
          alt="A weathered notice tallying Oklahoma's thousands of abandoned well sites."
          class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ CLIMATE ============================ -->
  <section
    id="climate"
    class="scroll-mt-32 border-t border-white/10 bg-black/30 px-6 pt-14 pb-12 sm:pt-32"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.4em] text-[var(--color-red)] uppercase">
        Crime Two
      </p>
      <h2
        class="mt-4 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-5xl leading-[0.95] tracking-tight sm:text-7xl"
      >
        Climate Crimes
      </h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black/30 px-6 pb-12">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-12 text-center sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <p
          class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-6xl tracking-tight text-[var(--color-red)] sm:text-7xl"
        >
          16,000
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[10px] tracking-[0.3em] text-white/50 uppercase">
          Abandoned wells left spewing methane
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p
          class="font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-6xl tracking-tight text-[var(--color-red)] sm:text-7xl"
        >
          8,000%
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[10px] tracking-[0.3em] text-white/50 uppercase">
          More damaging to the climate than CO₂
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black/30 px-6 pb-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
      <p>
        After Koch and Big Oil &mdash; Getty, Sinclair and Exxon &mdash; sucked
        billions of dollars in petroleum from the Osage Reservation, they left
        the Tribe with 16,000 abandoned wells spewing chemicals and methane.
        There is nothing worse than methane when it comes to global warming
        &mdash; 8,000% more damaging than CO₂.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="relative my-12">
    <img
      src="/pumpjack-windfarm.jpg"
      alt="A lone pump jack in a green field beneath a wind farm and storm-grey sky."
      class="h-[45vh] w-full object-cover sm:h-[65vh]"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </figure>

  <section class="bg-black/30 px-6 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
      <blockquote
        class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-red)] pl-6 font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-2xl leading-snug text-white italic sm:text-3xl"
      >
        &ldquo;Now how do you allow a company to just walk away like that?&rdquo;
        <cite
          class="mt-4 block font-[family-name:var(--font-body)] text-[10px] tracking-[0.3em] text-white/50 not-italic uppercase"
        >
          — Everett Waller, Chairman, Osage Minerals Council
        </cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        It's against the law. But there's the law, and there's oil. When shown
        the tape of Charlie Koch's concealed confession to the theft, Waller
        said:
      </p>
      <blockquote
        class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-red)] pl-6 font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-2xl leading-snug text-white italic sm:text-3xl"
      >
        &ldquo;I hope he enjoys those comments in hell. The greed just takes you
        over like a drug.&rdquo;
        <cite
          class="mt-4 block font-[family-name:var(--font-body)] text-[10px] tracking-[0.3em] text-white/50 not-italic uppercase"
        >
          — Everett Waller
        </cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black/30 px-6 pb-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
      <p>
        Waller and Chief Standing Bear are blocked from cleaning the filth on
        their lands by a campaign &mdash; funded by a half billion from the
        Kochs &mdash; to say that global warming &ldquo;is a hoax.&rdquo; What
        you see on the Osage Reservation is hardly a hoax. It is a horror show,
        an environmental crime only recently made legal. As Greg Palast, the
        investigative reporter who's hunted the Kochs for decades, explains:
      </p>
      <blockquote
        class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-red)] pl-6 font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-2xl leading-snug text-white italic sm:text-3xl"
      >
        &ldquo;My mob-boss uncle once told me: the best crime is the one you
        make legal.&rdquo;
        <cite
          class="mt-4 block font-[family-name:var(--font-body)] text-[10px] tracking-[0.3em] text-white/50 not-italic uppercase"
        >
          — Greg Palast
        </cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        We'll show you how Charlie & Co. pulled it off. Who will win this
        showdown &mdash; the Kochs or the Osage? &ldquo;Grandfather Sun,&rdquo;
        as Standing Bear says, needs to know. The Chief, a militant trial
        lawyer, is not waiting to find out. He's filing lawsuits and leading a
        campaign to take back control of his Nation's property &mdash; now
        lorded over by the Bureau of Indian Affairs &mdash; and to close up the
        earth-destroying methane belching into the atmosphere.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-white/10 bg-black/30 px-6 py-14 sm:py-24 text-center">
    <p
      class="mx-auto max-w-4xl font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-3xl leading-tight text-white italic sm:text-5xl"
    >
      &ldquo;Let's not beat around the bush.
      <span class="block text-[var(--color-red)] sm:mt-3">
        This is occupied territory.&rdquo;
      </span>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-8 text-[10px] tracking-[0.3em] text-white/50 uppercase">
      — Principal Chief Geoffrey Standing Bear
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== KILLERS OF THE FLOWER MOON ===================== -->
  <section id="flower-moon" class="scroll-mt-32 px-6 pt-14 pb-12 sm:pt-32">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-xs tracking-[0.4em] text-[var(--color-red)] uppercase">
        Crime Three
      </p>
      <h2
        class="mt-4 font-[family-name:var(--font-display)] text-4xl leading-[0.95] tracking-tight sm:text-6xl"
      >
        The Crimes of the<br />Killers of the Flower Moon
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
        In the 1870s, starvation and smallpox killed 90% of the tribe. After oil
        was discovered, by 1919 the Osage had become, per capita, the richest
        people in the world. Then the killings began.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
        <em class="text-[var(--color-bone)]">Long Knife</em> is the documentary
        sequel to <cite>Killers of the Flower Moon</cite>, the Martin Scorsese
        masterpiece about the 200 Osage murdered for their oil. Long Knife
        uncovers hard facts about this Reign of Terror, unearthed in this new
        investigation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 pb-12">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-px bg-white/10 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/archival-henry-roan.jpg"
          alt="Archival newspaper headline reporting the frozen body of Henry Roan found shot through the head."
          class="aspect-video w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/archival-skull-testimony.jpg"
          alt="Archival newspaper headline: a skull shown as testimony in an Osage case."
          class="aspect-video w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/archival-indian-baby.jpg"
          alt="Archival newspaper headline reporting an Osage infant among the victims."
          class="aspect-video w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 py-12 text-center">
    <blockquote
      class="mx-auto max-w-3xl font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-3xl leading-tight text-white italic sm:text-4xl"
    >
      &ldquo;There are all these little baby graves out there.&rdquo;
      <cite
        class="mt-6 block font-[family-name:var(--font-body)] text-[10px] tracking-[0.3em] text-white/50 not-italic uppercase"
      >
        — Mogri Lookout, Osage Elder
      </cite>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
      <p>
        How do you get away with cold-blooded murder day after day? Because
        killing an Indian on the Osage was not considered a crime until 1924.
        History is ever-present. The crimes of the Kochs were foretold in the
        Trail of Tears, which ended with the Osage expulsion from Kansas after
        the robber baron Jay Gould convinced Congress to let him buy the Osage
        reservation for just <strong class="text-[var(--color-bone)]"
          >12 cents an acre</strong
        >. It was a scandal even then.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="relative my-12">
    <img
      src="/archival-osage-ancestor.jpg"
      alt="A treated sepia portrait of an Osage ancestor on the prairie."
      class="h-[45vh] w-full object-cover sm:h-[65vh]"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </figure>

  <section class="px-6 py-12">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/85 sm:text-xl">
      <p>
        In Oklahoma, Chief Bigheart wrote down their Constitution, in which the
        Chief was democratically elected and all land held in common. The U.S.
        Congress revoked their Constitution, replaced Bigheart with a council of
        oil men, and chopped up their land into 2,000 parcels &mdash; the easier
        to steal and cheat the Osage out of their oil. And to kill those who
        resisted.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a century, until 2006, the oil men ruled over the Osage and turned a
        blind eye to Koch's burglaries. Congress forced the Osage to sell their
        oil rights. J. Paul Getty became the richest man in the world from the
        oil land he bought from the Osage for $500.
      </p>
      <p
        class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-red)] pl-6 font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-2xl text-white italic sm:text-3xl"
      >
        The Kochs invented nothing new.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 pb-24">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-5xl gap-px bg-white/10 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/archival-chief-black-dog.jpg"
          alt="A sepia studio portrait of Chief Black Dog and his wife, Pawhuska, Oklahoma."
          class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/archival-indian-termination.jpg"
          alt="An archival newspaper op-ed on the federal Indian Termination policy."
          class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <figure class="bg-[var(--color-ink)]">
        <img
          src="/archival-oil-derrick.jpg"
          alt="An early oil derrick silhouetted against billowing black smoke at dusk."
          class="aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Close / CTA -->
  <section class="border-t border-white/10 px-6 py-14 sm:py-24 text-center">
    <p
      class="mx-auto max-w-3xl font-[family-name:var(--font-quote)] text-2xl leading-tight italic sm:text-4xl"
    >
      Behind every great fortune is a great crime.
      <span class="block text-[var(--color-red)] sm:mt-3">This is the crime.</span>
    </p>
    <div class="mt-12">
      <a
        href="/#support"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 border border-[var(--color-bone)] px-8 py-4 text-xs tracking-[0.3em] uppercase transition-colors hover:bg-[var(--color-bone)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]"
      >
        Support the Film
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
